        <groundspeak:log id="633230153">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-08-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1685537">nosweat6060</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP490 Aberdeen St&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Was with Team DJM doing a little caching in Medicine Hat. He showed me this Cap while looking for a nearby cache. After finding the Cap we stopped at a small lemonade stand run by two young entrepreneurs. Refreshing drink on a hot day! Thanks for all the Brass Caps. Great fun.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="630767181">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-08-20T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7364793">NurseB33</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP490 Aberdeen St&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Happy International Geocaching Day &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Geo-Mom and I are in town for SAW XII (and general geocaching) and this time I came organized with a list of Brass Caps in the area &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_approve.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;! Following the S7: Flash Mob (super fun), I headed downtown for the Wherigo cache and to grab some Brass Caps. This one was easy to spot and details have been sent to the C.O. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for another great Brass Cap, OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
